# Editor-only type stubs written by the portal build, one pair per Vite root.
# createPortalConfig() calls frappeui(), whose lucideIcons() option defaults ON and
# registers unplugin-auto-import + unplugin-vue-components; each writes its own
# .d.ts next to the portal's vite.config.js on every `npm run build`. Nothing in the
# tree imports them and there is no tsconfig.json or vue-tsc step anywhere under
# frontend/, so they are build output that only an editor reads.
#
# This is the line between the two kinds of generated artefact here: the portal
# bundles under apex/public/<portal>/ stay TRACKED because the app must install on a
# site with no Node toolchain, while these stubs ship to nobody and are rewritten
# byte-identically by the next build.
auto-imports.d.ts
components.d.ts
.vite/
